text She hides her face. She must be blushing.
text ...She probably wants to add, "Thanks to you."
text I only now realize how masochistic my confession was.
text I never wanted her to touch that scar.
text I can feel my face getting red.
text @[Tomoya]
text I see.
text @[Tomoya]
text It'd be nice if that could happen...
text So I look up at the sky.
text It shines silver beyond the roofs of the town's buildings.
text I wait for the wind to blow on my face and cool me down.
text ...Three years ago.
text Life at school was going great for me. I was captain of the basketball team.
text Because of my athletics, I pretty much had any and every high school open to me to choose from. So the plan was to pick a good one and keep playing basketball once I got there.
text But that path was suddenly cut off.
text It was because of the fight I had with my father.
text It started over my appearance, or maybe it was how my shoes were messy by the front door... Either way, it was something stupid like that.
text Regardless, we started shoving each other, which eventually escalated things into a fight...
text Then I hit my right shoulder against the wall...
text No matter how intense the pain got, I stayed stubborn. I just shut myself in my room, refusing to do anything about it.
text By the time I did go to a doctor, it was already too late...
text I'd never be able to raise my arm above my shoulder again.
setvar intF[9] = 1
